adjudication.rationale:
In `packages/core/EventManager.ts` `createAllCalendarEvents`, the logic was changed from a single credential-less fan-out to running inside `for (const destination of event.destinationCalendar)`. For destinations without `credentialId`, it executes:

```ts
const destinationCalendarCredentials = this.calendarCredentials.filter(c => c.type === destination.integration);
createdEvents = createdEvents.concat(
  await Promise.all(destinationCalendarCredentials.map(c => createEvent(c, event)))
);
```

This means if `event.destinationCalendar` contains multiple entries lacking `credentialId` (e.g., legacy rows), the same set of matching credentials will be used repeatedly, creating duplicate events (one full fan-out per destination entry). Additionally, this branch calls `createEvent(c, event)` without the new `externalId` argument, so `CalendarManager.createEvent` returns `externalId: undefined`, and downstream reference construction now uses `externalCalendarId: result.externalId`, yielding references with `externalCalendarId` undefined. For Google, `createEvent` selects a calendar by matching `credentialId`; when absent, it falls back to `primary`, reinforcing the “duplicates on primary” outcome. This is a real defect introduced by the diff.
